  "question": {
    "text": "A wire of length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo> </mo><mi>cm</mi></math> and radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mn>7</mn></msqrt><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> connected across the right gap of a meter bridge. When a resistance of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi></math> is connected on the left gap by using a resistance box, the balance length is found to be at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>60</mn><mo> </mo><mi>cm</mi></math> from the left end. If the resistivity of the wire is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></msup><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>, then value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math> is :",
    "image": null
  },
